L724: 17b For binary outcomes, presentation of both absolute and relative effect sizes is recommended           Ancillary analyses 18 Results of any other analyses performed, including subgroup analyses and adjusted analyses, distinguishing pre-specified from exploratory
L725: Harms 19 All important harms or unintended effects in each group (for specific guidance see CONSORT for harms)
L726: **Discussion**
L727: Limitations 20 Trial limitations, addressing sources of potential bias, imprecision, and, if relevant, multiplicity of analyses 8-9
L728: Generalisability 21 Generalisability (external validity, applicability) of the trial findings 8-9
L729: Interpretation 22 Interpretation consistent with results, balancing benefits and harms, and considering other relevant evidence 8-9
L730: **Other information**
L731: Registration 23 Registration number and name of trial registry Protocol 24 Where the full trial protocol can be accessed, if available Funding 25 Sources of funding and other support (such as supply of drugs), role of funders 10
L732: - We strongly recommend reading this statement in conjunction with the CONSORT 2010 Explanation and Elaboration for important clarifications on all the items. If relevant, we also
L733: recommend reading CONSORT extensions for cluster randomised trials, non-inferiority and equivalence trials, non-pharmacological treatments, herbal interventions, and pragmatic trials.
L734: Additional extensions are forthcoming: for those and for up to date references relevant to this checklist, see www.consort-statement.org.
